<title>CANADA: CanWest won't appeal WIC ruling.</title>
<headline>CanWest won't appeal WIC ruling.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>CanWest Global Communications Corp said Thursday it will not appeal a court ruling in a case involving rival broadcaster WIC Western International Communications Ltd.</p>
<p>CanWest and two former WIC directors had appealed a lower court ruling that effectively blocked CanWest's C$636 million takeover bid for WIC last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Our position is it's time to move on. We will not appeal,&quot; CanWest vice president of corporate development Leonard Asper said in an interview. He said CanWest plans to hold its 15 percent stake in WIC's non-voting Class B shares.</p>
</text>
